tion errors described in chapter 16. UI never parses exception strings to decide behavior.\n\nLong-running calls return a Job ID immediately.\n\n## SourceService\n\nRequired operations:\n\n~~~python\nadd_source(path: Path, display_name: str | None = None) -> Source\nremove_source(source_id: UUID) -> None\nset_enabled(source_id: UUID, enabled: bool) -> None\nupdate_exclusions(source_id: UUID, rules: list[ExclusionRule]) -> ExclusionPreview\nscan(source_id: UUID, mode: ScanMode = INCREMENTAL) -> JobId\nget(source_id: UUID) -> Source\nlist() -> list[Source]\n~~~\n\nRemoving a Source removes Koffer indexing state according to explicit UI confirmation but never deletes its directory/audio.\n\n## SearchService\n\n~~~python\nsearch(query: SampleQuery, page: PageRequest) -> Page[SampleRow]\ncount(query: SampleQuery) -> int\nsave_search(name: str, query: SampleQuery) -> SavedSearch\nupdate_saved_search(id: UUID, ...) -> SavedSearch\ndelete_saved_search(id: UUID) -> None\n~~~\n\nSampleQuery is a typed versioned representation of S02 filters.\n\n## CollectionService\n\n~~~python\ncreate(name: str, description: str | None = None) -> Collection\nupdate(id: UUID, ...) -> Collection\ndelete(id: UUID) -> None\nadd_samples(collection_id: UUID, sample_ids: list[UUID]) -> None\nremove_samples(collection_id: UUID, sample_ids: list[UUID]) -> None\nreorder(collection_id: UUID, ordered_sample_ids: list[UUID]) -> None\n~~~\n\n==> /home/sean/Documents/experiments/csw-041026/koffer/docs/04-browsing-search-and-collections.md <==\n# 4. Browsing, Search, and Collections\n\n## Search\nSearch should be fast enough to remain the primary way to locate sounds.\n\nUsers should be able to search by filename, file extension/type, Sample Type, Instrument/Source, Role, Genre/Style, Character, BPM, Key, duration, technical properties, user tags, and Collections.\n\n## Faceted filters\nSearch results can be narrowed through visible facets such as One-shot, Loop, Phrase, Stem, Track, Drum, Bass, Vocal, Synth, BPM ranges, key/mode, Mono, and Stereo.\n\nFilters should combine rather than replace one another.\n\n## Results\nUseful result columns may include name, Sample Type, Instrument/Source, BPM, Key, duration, format, Collection state, and suggestion/review state.\n\nThe user should be able to choose which columns are visible.\n\n## Sorting\nResults should support sorting by name, duration, BPM, key, date discovered, last used, file size, and analysis confidence.\n\n## Collections\nCollections are intentional groups of Samples.\n\nExamples:\n- Favourite Breaks\n- MPC Export\n- Vinyl Chops\n- Field Recordings\n- Drum Machine Gold\n\nA Sample may belong to multiple Collections without creating multiple copies.\n\n## Favourites and recents\nKoffer should provide quick access to favourites, recently previewed, recently added, and recently modified/prepared Samples.\n\n## Saved searches\nA filtered query may be saved as a reusable view.\n\nExample: One-shot + Kick + Electronic + duration under 1 second.\n\nSaved searches remain dynamic as new matching Samples are discovered.\n\n## Similar sounds\nWhere audio embeddings are available, the user may choose **Find Similar** on a Sample.\n\nSimilarity search is separate from metadata search: it asks which Samples sound related even when filenames and tags differ.\nkoffer\n","stderr":"","executionTime":855,"interleavedOutput":"total 140\ndrwxrwxr-x 10 sean sean  4096 Oct  4 14:49 .\ndrwxrwxr-x  8 sean sean  4096 Oct  4 14:49 ..\ndrwxrwxr-x  3 sean sean  4096 Oct  4 14:49 docs\ndrwxrwxr-x  8 sean sean  4096 Oct  4 14:49 .git\ndrwxrwxr-x  3 sean sean  4096 Oct  4 14:49 .github\n-rw-rw-r--  1 sean sean   267 Oct  4 14:49 .gitignore\ndrwxrwxr-x  2 sean sean  4096 Oct  4 14:49 .grapher\n-rw-rw-r--  1 sean sean  1065 Oct  4 14:49 LICENSE\n-rw-rw-r--  1 sean sean   409 Oct  4 14:49 Makefile\ndrwxrwxr-x  4 sean sean  4096 Oct  4 14:49 packaging\n-rw-rw-r--  1 sean sean  1227 Oct  4 14:49 pyproject.toml\n-rw-rw-r--  1 sean sean  1572 Oc